om agent configuration directories (.claude/, .codex/, .gemini/). These directories may contain API keys, personal settings, and other credentials that the skill has no legitimate need to access.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-c42dce8557974743bd679ef079739627","line":118,"path":"SKILL.md","start_column":3}],"path":"SKILL.md","pattern":"Agent Config Directory Access","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Remove all code or instructions that access agent configuration directories (.claude/, .codex/, .gemini/). If configuration values are needed, pass them explicitly as parameters or environment variables — never read the agent's own config files.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"AS1","severity":"HIGH","start_column":3,"tags":["Agent Snooping"]},{"category":"Excessive Agency","code_snippet":"\nSteps 1, 2 and 3 are the **wrap path**: a live agent calling tools freely,\nwith the recorder in front of it and `policy.yml` as its seatbelt. Nothing in\nthat path involves a `skill.md`, and no approval exists there.\n\nStep 4 is the **replay path**: a frozen, ordered step list in a\n`<name>.skill.md` file that `reelier run` executes with no model in the loop.","confidence":0.75,"evidence":{},"finding":"no approval","finding_ids":["finding-fac2fbefa2bc4453b83560135b934528"],"id":"sha256:a818a4bf8b106d68c9cae71f3366f6aee5bf1cb3a51f388d7cdc5c584e4b28a1","intent":null,"line":159,"match_fingerprint":"02114119728c4c9031d411902239e1c4b76f46eb7c1932c9ae63fcbe2fd1030c","message":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-fac2fbefa2bc4453b83560135b934528","line":159,"path":"SKILL.md","start_column":37}],"path":"SKILL.md","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"EA2","severity":"MEDIUM","start_column":37,"tags":["Excessive Agency"]},{"category":"Rogue Agent","code_snippet":"before touching it**, and it is idempotent.\n\n**Do not run `install` yourself.** It edits the user's agent configuration on\ntheir machine. Show them the command, say what it will rewrite and that a\nbackup is written first, and let them run it.\n\nState these four gaps whenever you show this command. Each one is a server","confidence":0.6,"evidence":{},"finding":"write and that a\nbackup is written first, and let them run it.\n\nState these four gaps whenever you show this command. Each one is a server\nthat keeps running unwrapped, so a receipt cannot speak for i","finding_ids":["finding-598b7529ef20456eb642bcda2a38aebb"],"id":"sha256:c7181dd5bafe440efe138d0525239ec9ae87bcc170c596c9bf8b7ebbc9ac7d28","intent":null,"line":111,"match_fingerprint":"9fb8b266c35bf735e9a9beeb8c069fb7765d0afd17c8cec239e50133bdb2e31f","message":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-598b7529ef20456eb642bcda2a38aebb","line":111,"path":"SKILL.md","start_column":57}],"path":"SKILL.md","pattern":"Session Persistence","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"RA2","severity":"MEDIUM","start_column":57,"tags":["Rogue Agent"]},{"category":"MCP Rug Pull","code_snippet":null,"confidence":0.7,"evidence":{},"finding":null,"finding_ids":["finding-2d16ef0b6f3847feafb82b8b3f662984","finding-af54a7e62a834d62b34ff9c359370a9f","finding-9d3d8dd3df924e97b4db9ac645459bd2","finding-05e2e940d0db4f7f82533304e